{"at":"2026-10-13T09:49:35.632Z","tool":"submit_plan","args":"{\"issue\":99002,\"plan\":\"# Text properties\\nupdate C-001: a two-line text at line height \\\"Loose\\\" (1.5) keeps 1.5 and \\\"Loose\\\" stays highlighted after the font family changes; the existing checks stay\\ncreate TC-1: \\\"Line height\\\" presets \\\"Tight\\\", \\\"Normal\\\" and \\\"Loose\\\" on a multi-line text\\ncre","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T09:51:10.219Z","tool":"save_changes","args":"{\"issue\":99002,\"content\":\"Scope: line height control for text (desktop Chrome, Firefox and Safari, plus the mobile layout at 375 px). To read an exact line height, select the text and read the value in the \\\"Line height\\\" field. Presets are \\\"Tight\\\" = 1.0, \\\"Normal\\\" = 1.25 and \\\"Loose\\\" = 1.5; the","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T09:51:15.149Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"text-properties\",\"fact\":\"The \\\"Line height\\\" control in the properties panel has presets \\\"Tight\\\" = 1.0, \\\"Normal\\\" = 1.25 and \\\"Loose\\\" = 1.5 plus a field that accepts a typed value from 0.8 to 2.5 in steps of 0.05; it is shown when a text, a shape with text or an arrow label is selected ","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T09:51:16.702Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"text-properties\",\"fact\":\"In the \\\"Line height\\\" field, values below 0.8 become 0.8, values above 2.5 become 2.5, values between steps round to the nearest 0.05, both \\\".\\\" and \\\",\\\" work as decimal separator, and empty or non-numeric input keeps the previous value.\",\"source\":\"Approved answe","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T09:51:18.352Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"text-properties\",\"fact\":\"New text keeps its font's own line height until a line height is chosen, after which the last chosen value is the default for new text; a chosen line height is kept when the font family changes, while a never-changed text follows its new font's own line height.\",\"so","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T09:51:19.904Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"text-properties\",\"fact\":\"With several texts at different line heights selected, no \\\"Line height\\\" preset is highlighted and the field is empty; a preset click or a typed value sets that line height on all of them, and a value matching no preset highlights no preset.\",\"source\":\"Approved ans","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T09:51:21.553Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"bound-text\",\"fact\":\"Changing the line height of text inside a shape changes the shape's height while its width stays the same; an arrow label stays at the middle of the arrow; a sticky note's auto-fit takes line height into account so the label never overflows the note.\",\"source\":\"Approved ","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T09:51:23.061Z","tool":"propose_knowledge","args":"{\"area\":\"files-and-export\",\"fact\":\"A text's line height survives a page reload, a saved .excalidraw file, PNG and SVG export, live collaboration, paste styles, copies and undo/redo; behavior in older Excalidraw versions is out of scope.\",\"source\":\"Approved answers 9 and 10 in the issue 99002 session","outcome":"ok"}
